IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa2-part7-other-routes.l4: Part 7 (Re-registration as a means of altering a company's status), the other four routes,
-- ss 97-111, lines 1226-1413 of ukpga-2006-46.txt: public to private (97-101), private limited to unlimited (102-104),
-- unlimited to limited (105-108), public to unlimited private (109-111).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; no point of view.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text".  Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes.   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words.
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seams taken as inputs: s 283 "special resolution" (coa7), s 1121 "officer in default" (coa24), s 1146 "authenticated" (coa25),
-- s 1167 "prescribed" (keel), s 10 and Chapter 3 of Part 3 (coa1), s 4(1), s 4(2), s 3(1)-(4) (keel; plain BOOLEAN).
-- Every name that is not in coa-core.l4 begins with the section label it implements.

-- A conjunction of MAYBE BOOLEAN answers that keeps "not covered": any JUST FALSE makes it JUST FALSE, otherwise any
-- NOTHING makes it NOTHING.
-- src:1227 | 97 Re-registration of public company as private limited company
-- src:1228 | (1) A public company may be re-registered as a private limited company if—
-- src:1229 | (a) a special resolution that it should be so re-registered is passed,
-- src:1230 | (b) the conditions specified below are met, and
-- src:1231 | (c) an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 100, together with—
-- src:1232 | (i) the other documents required by that section, and
-- src:1233 | (ii) a statement of compliance.
@ref s 97(1) Re-registration of public company as private limited company (the conditions together) (src:1227-1233)
GIVEN answers IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97(1) all of the answers hold` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN answer YIELD answer EQUALS JUST FALSE) answers
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the "if" that introduces the conditions of the calling section ("A public company may be re-registered as a private limited company if— (a) ..., (b) ..., and (c) ...", likewise ss 105(1) and 109(1))
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN answer YIELD answer EQUALS NOTHING) answers
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): an answer another section gives is not known
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Public company becoming private (ss 97-101)
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:1234 | (2) The conditions are that—
-- src:1235 | (a) where no application under section 98 for cancellation of the resolution has been made—
-- src:1236 | (i) having regard to the number of members who consented to or voted in favour of the resolution, no such application may be made, or
-- src:1237 | (ii) the period within which such an application could be made has expired, or
-- src:1238 | (b) where such an application has been made—
-- src:1239 | (i) the application has been withdrawn, or
-- src:1240 | (ii) an order has been made confirming the resolution and a copy of that order has been delivered to the registrar.
@ref s 97(2) The conditions (src:1234-1240)
GIVEN `an application under section 98 for the cancellation of the resolution has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `having regard to the number of members who consented to or voted in favour of the resolution, no such application may be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period within which such an application could be made has expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application has been withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order has been made confirming the resolution and a copy of that order has been delivered to the registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97(2) the conditions are met` MEANS
    IF NOT (`an application under section 98 for the cancellation of the resolution has been made`)
    THEN IF       `having regard to the number of members who consented to or voted in favour of the resolution, no such application may be made`
              OR  `the period within which such an application could be made has expired`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The conditions are that— (a) where no application under section 98 for cancellation of the resolution has been made— (i) ... or (ii) ..."
    ELSE IF       `the application has been withdrawn`
              OR  `an order has been made confirming the resolution and a copy of that order has been delivered to the registrar`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where such an application has been made— (i) the application has been withdrawn, or (ii) an order has been made confirming the resolution and a copy of that order has been delivered to the registrar"

-- src:1227 | 97 Re-registration of public company as private limited company
-- src:1228 | (1) A public company may be re-registered as a private limited company if—
-- src:1229 | (a) a special resolution that it should be so re-registered is passed,
-- src:1230 | (b) the conditions specified below are met, and
-- src:1231 | (c) an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 100, together with—
-- src:1232 | (i) the other documents required by that section, and
-- src:1233 | (ii) a statement of compliance.
@ref s 97(1) Re-registration of public company as private limited company (src:1227-1233)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 97(2) the conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 100, together with the other documents required by that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of compliance is delivered together with the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97(1) the public company may be re-registered as a private limited company` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(2) the company is a public company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company may be re-registered"
    ELSE
        `s 97(1) all of the answers hold`
            (LIST   `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution`
                  , `s 97(2) the conditions are met`
                  , (IF `an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 100, together with the other documents required by that section` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
                  , (IF `a statement of compliance is delivered together with the application` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE))

-- src:1241 | (3) The company must make such changes—
-- src:1242 | (a) in its name, and
@ref s 97(3)(a) The company must change its name (src:1241-1242)
GIVEN `the company is being re-registered as a private limited company under section 97` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97(3)(a) the company must make such changes in its name as are necessary in connection with its becoming a private company limited by shares or by guarantee` MEANS
    IF `the company is being re-registered as a private limited company under section 97`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's becoming a private company limited by shares or by guarantee on this re-registration

-- src:1241 | (3) The company must make such changes—
-- src:1243 | (b) in its articles,
-- src:1244 | as are necessary in connection with its becoming a private company limited by shares or, as the case may be, by guarantee.
@ref s 97(3)(b) The company must change its articles (src:1241-1244)
GIVEN `the company is being re-registered as a private limited company under section 97` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 97(3)(b) the company must make such changes in its articles as are necessary in connection with its becoming a private company limited by shares or by guarantee` MEANS
    IF `the company is being re-registered as a private limited company under section 97`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's becoming a private company limited by shares or by guarantee on this re-registration

DECLARE `s 98(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 98(2) apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution`

-- src:1245 | 98 Application to court to cancel resolution
-- src:1246 | (1) Where a special resolution by a public company to be re-registered as a private limited company has been passed, an application to the court for the cancellation of the resolution may be made—
-- src:1247 | (a) by the holders of not less in the aggregate than 5% in nominal value of the company's issued share capital or any class of the company's issued share capital (disregarding any shares held by the company as treasury shares);
-- src:1248 | (b) if the company is not limited by shares, by not less than 5% of its members; or
-- src:1249 | (c) by not less than 50 of the company's members;
-- src:1250 | but not by a person who has consented to or voted in favour of the resolution.
@ref s 98(1) Application to court to cancel resolution (src:1245-1250)
GIVEN `a special resolution by a public company to be re-registered as a private limited company has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the nominal value of the issued share capital (or of the class) held by the applicants` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the company's issued share capital (or of the class), disregarding any shares held by the company as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members who are applicants` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the company's members` IS A NUMBER
      `any of the applicants has consented to or voted in favour of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(1) the applicants may apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a special resolution by a public company to be re-registered as a private limited company has been passed`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a special resolution by a public company to be re-registered as a private limited company has been passed, an application to the court for the cancellation of the resolution may be made"
    ELSE IF `any of the applicants has consented to or voted in favour of the resolution`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but not by a person who has consented to or voted in favour of the resolution"
         ELSE IF       `the nominal value of the issued share capital (or of the class) held by the applicants` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the nominal value of the company's issued share capital (or of the class), disregarding any shares held by the company as treasury shares` -- (a) not less in the aggregate than 5%
                  OR   ((NOT (`the company is limited by shares`)) AND `the number of members who are applicants` TIMES 20 AT LEAST `the number of the company's members`) -- (b) not limited by shares: not less than 5% of its members
                  OR   `the number of members who are applicants` AT LEAST 50 -- (c) not less than 50 of the company's members
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be made— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." names three kinds of applicant and does not say that no other may apply

-- src:1251 | (2) The application must be made within 28 days after the passing of the resolution and may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make it by such one or more of their number as they may appoint for the purpose.
@ref s 98(2) The application must be made within 28 days after the passing of the resolution (src:1251-1251)
GIVEN `the date on which the resolution is passed` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the application is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(2) the application is made within 28 days after the passing of the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the application is made` AT MOST (`the date on which the resolution is passed` PLUS 28)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be made within 28 days after the passing of the resolution"

-- src:1251 | (2) The application must be made within 28 days after the passing of the resolution and may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make it by such one or more of their number as they may appoint for the purpose.
@ref s 98(2) The permission to apply, within 28 days (src:1251-1251)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 98(2) act`
`s 98(2) the members' permission to apply to the court` MEANS
    PARTY Member
    MAY `s 98(2) apply to the court for the cancellation of the resolution`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1251 | (2) The application must be made within 28 days after the passing of the resolution and may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make it by such one or more of their number as they may appoint for the purpose.
@ref s 98(2) The application may be made on behalf of those entitled by one or more of their number (src:1251-1251)
GIVEN `the application is made on behalf of the persons entitled to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by one or more of their number whom they appoint for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(2) the application may be made on behalf of the persons entitled to make it` MEANS
    IF `the application is made on behalf of the persons entitled to make it` AND `it is made by one or more of their number whom they appoint for the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such one or more of their number as they may appoint for the purpose"

-- src:1252 | (3) On the hearing of the application the court shall make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution.
@ref s 98(3) The court shall make an order cancelling or confirming (src:1252-1252)
GIVEN `the application is heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(3) the court shall make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution` MEANS
    IF `the application is heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the hearing of the application the court shall make an order either cancelling or confirming the resolution."

-- src:1253 | (4) The court may—
-- src:1254 | (a) make that order on such terms and conditions as it thinks fit,
-- src:1255 | (b) if it thinks fit adjourn the proceedings in order that an arrangement may be made to the satisfaction of the court for the purchase of the interests of dissentient members, and
-- src:1256 | (c) give such directions, and make such orders, as it thinks expedient for facilitating or carrying into effect any such arrangement.
@ref s 98(4) The court's powers on the hearing (src:1253-1256)
GIVEN `the application is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(4) the court may make the order on terms, adjourn for the purchase of dissentient members' interests, and give directions` MEANS
    IF `the application is being heard`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ..." on the hearing of the application

-- src:1257 | (5) The court's order may, if the court thinks fit—
-- src:1258 | (a) provide for the purchase by the company of the shares of any of its members and for the reduction accordingly of the company's capital; and
-- src:1259 | (b) make such alteration in the company's articles as may be required in consequence of that provision.
@ref s 98(5) The court's order may provide for a purchase of shares and an alteration of the articles (src:1257-1259)
GIVEN `the court makes an order on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(5) the court's order may provide for the purchase by the company of members' shares and alter the articles` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order on the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court's order may, if the court thinks fit— (a) ... (b) ..."

-- src:1260 | (6) The court's order may, if the court thinks fit, require the company not to make any, or any specified, amendments to its articles without the leave of the court.
@ref s 98(6) The court's order may require the company not to amend its articles without leave (src:1260-1260)
GIVEN `the court makes an order on the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(6) the court's order may require the company not to amend its articles without the leave of the court` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order on the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court's order may, if the court thinks fit, require the company not to make any, or any specified, amendments to its articles without the leave of the court."

-- src:1261 | (7) In this section and section 99(3) “the court”, in England and Wales, means the High Court
@ref s 98(7) "the court" in England and Wales means the High Court (src:1261-1261)
GIVEN `the place where the application is made` IS A `Place of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 98(7) the court is the High Court` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place where the application is made`
    WHEN `England and Wales` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): as rendered the subsection says only "in England and Wales, means the High Court" (finding 5)

-- src:1262 | 99 Notice to registrar of court application or order
-- src:1263 | (1) On making an application under section 98 (application to court to cancel resolution) the applicants, or the person making the application on their behalf, must immediately give notice to the registrar.
-- src:1264 | This is without prejudice to any provision of rules of court as to service of notice of the application.
@ref s 99(1) The applicants must immediately give notice to the registrar (src:1262-1264)
GIVEN `an application is made under section 98` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99(1) the applicants must immediately give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `an application is made under section 98`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On making an application under section 98 ... the applicants, or the person making the application on their behalf, must immediately give notice to the registrar."

-- src:1262 | 99 Notice to registrar of court application or order
-- src:1265 | (2) On being served with notice of any such application, the company must immediately give notice to the registrar.
@ref s 99(2) The company must immediately give notice to the registrar (src:1262-1265)
GIVEN `the company is served with notice of an application under section 98` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99(2) the company must immediately give notice to the registrar` MEANS
    IF `the company is served with notice of an application under section 98`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On being served with notice of any such application, the company must immediately give notice to the registrar."

-- src:1266 | (3) Within 15 days of the making of the court's order on the application, or such longer period as the court may at any time direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order.
@ref s 99(3) The days allowed for delivering a copy of the order (src:1266-1266)
GIVEN `the longer period the court directs, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 99(3) the number of days allowed for delivering a copy of the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the longer period the court directs, in days`
    WHEN JUST directed THEN IF directed GREATER THAN 15 THEN directed ELSE 15 -- "such longer period": a direction of 15 days or fewer adds nothing
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 15

-- src:1266 | (3) Within 15 days of the making of the court's order on the application, or such longer period as the court may at any time direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order.
@ref s 99(3) The copy of the order is delivered in time (src:1266-1266)
GIVEN `the date of the making of the court's order` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the copy of the order is delivered to the registrar` IS A DATE
      `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99(3) the copy of the order is delivered within the time allowed` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the copy of the order is delivered to the registrar` AT MOST (`the date of the making of the court's order` PLUS `the number of days allowed`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 15 days of the making of the court's order on the application, or such longer period as the court may at any time direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order."

DECLARE `s 99(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 99(3) deliver a copy of the order to the registrar`

-- src:1266 | (3) Within 15 days of the making of the court's order on the application, or such longer period as the court may at any time direct, the company must deliver to the registrar a copy of the order.
@ref s 99(3) The company's duty to deliver a copy of the order (src:1266-1266)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 99(3) act`
`s 99(3) the company's duty to deliver a copy of the order` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 99(3) deliver a copy of the order to the registrar`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company failed to deliver a copy of the court's order to the registrar in time: an offence is committed under section 99(4)"

-- src:1267 | (4) If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3) an offence is committed by—
-- src:1268 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1269 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 99(4) Failure to comply with (2) or (3): who commits the offence (src:1267-1269)
GIVEN `the company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 99(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with subsection (2) or (3) an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `Officer in default` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Director THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Company secretary` THEN `liability of an officer`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names the company and every officer in default; it has no sentence treating a shadow director as an officer here
    WHERE
        `liability of an officer` MEANS
            IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:1270 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 99(5) Offence (penalty) (src:1270-1270)
`s 99(5) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- src:1271 | 100 Application and accompanying documents
-- src:1272 | (1) An application for re-registration as a private limited company must contain a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration.
@ref s 100(1) The application must contain a statement of the proposed name (src:1271-1272)
GIVEN `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(1) the application contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for re-registration as a private limited company must contain a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration."

-- src:1271 | 100 Application and accompanying documents
-- src:1273 | (2) The application must be accompanied by—
-- src:1274 | (a) a copy of the resolution that the company should re-register as a private limited company (unless a copy has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3); and
-- src:1275 | (b) a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended.
@ref s 100(2) The application must be accompanied by (src:1271-1275)
GIVEN `a copy of the resolution that the company should re-register as a private limited company accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of that resolution has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(2) the application is accompanied by what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       (`a copy of the resolution that the company should re-register as a private limited company accompanies the application` OR `a copy of that resolution has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3`)
         AND `a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompanies the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be accompanied by— (a) ... (unless a copy has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3); and (b) ..."

-- src:1276 | (3) The statement of compliance required to be delivered together with the application is a statement that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a private limited company have been complied with.
@ref s 100(3) The statement of compliance (src:1276-1276)
GIVEN `the statement is that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a private limited company have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(3) the statement meets the description of the statement of compliance` MEANS
    IF `the statement is that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a private limited company have been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of compliance ... is a statement that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a private limited company have been complied with."

-- src:1277 | (4) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a private limited company.
@ref s 100(4) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance (src:1277-1277)
GIVEN `a statement of compliance has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 100(4) the registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a private limited company` MEANS
    IF `a statement of compliance has been delivered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may accept the statement of compliance"; there is none

-- ---- s 101: issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration -----------------------------------

-- src:1278 | 101 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1279 | (1) If on an application for re-registration as a private limited company the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered, the company shall be re-registered accordingly.
@ref s 101(1) The company shall be re-registered (src:1278-1279)
GIVEN `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 101(1) the company shall be re-registered as a private limited company` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application for re-registration as a private limited company the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered, the company shall be re-registered accordingly."

-- src:1278 | 101 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
