`s 102(3)(b) the company must make such further changes as are necessary in connection with its becoming an unlimited company having a share capital` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company is being re-registered as an unlimited company under section 102`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's becoming an unlimited company on this re-registration
    ELSE IF `the company is to have a share capital`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if it is to have a share capital, as are necessary in connection with its becoming an unlimited company having a share capital"

