    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's becoming a company limited by shares or by guarantee on this re-registration

-- src:1332 | (4) The company must make such changes—
-- src:1334 | (b) in its articles,
-- src:1335 | as are necessary in connection with its becoming a company limited by shares or, as the case may be, by guarantee.
@ref s 105(4)(b) The company must change its articles (src:1332-1335)
GIVEN `the company is being re-registered as a private limited company under section 105` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(4)(b) the company must make such changes in its articles as are necessary in connection with its becoming a company limited by shares or by guarantee` MEANS
    IF `the company is being re-registered as a private limited company under section 105`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the company's becoming a company limited by shares or by guarantee on this re-registration

-- src:1336 | 106 Application and accompanying documents
-- src:1337 | (1) An application for re-registration as a limited company must contain a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration.
@ref s 106(1) The application must contain a statement of the proposed name (src:1336-1337)
GIVEN `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(1) the application contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the application contains a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An application for re-registration as a limited company must contain a statement of the company's proposed name on re-registration."

-- src:1336 | 106 Application and accompanying documents
-- src:1338 | (2) The application must be accompanied by—
-- src:1339 | (a) a copy of the resolution that the company should re-register as a private limited company (unless a copy has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3);
-- src:1340 | (b) if the company is to be limited by guarantee, a statement of guarantee;
-- src:1341 | (c) a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended.
@ref s 106(2) The application must be accompanied by (src:1336-1341)
GIVEN `a copy of the resolution that the company should re-register as a private limited company accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of that resolution has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is to be limited by guarantee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of guarantee accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompanies the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(2) the application is accompanied by what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       (`a copy of the resolution that the company should re-register as a private limited company accompanies the application` OR `a copy of that resolution has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3`)
         AND ((NOT (`the company is to be limited by guarantee`)) OR `a statement of guarantee accompanies the application`)
         AND `a copy of the company's articles as proposed to be amended accompanies the application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The application must be accompanied by— (a) ... (unless a copy has already been forwarded to the registrar under Chapter 3 of Part 3); (b) if the company is to be limited by guarantee, a statement of guarantee; (c) ..."

-- src:1342 | (3) The statement of guarantee required to be delivered in the case of a company that is to be limited by guarantee must state that each member undertakes that, if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member, he will contribute to the assets of the company such amount as may be required for—
-- src:1343 | (a) payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member,
-- src:1344 | (b) payment of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up, and
-- src:1345 | (c) adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves,
-- src:1346 | not exceeding a specified amount.
@ref s 106(3) The statement of guarantee: the member's undertaking (src:1342-1346)
GIVEN `the company is wound up while he is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which he ceases to be a member` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date on which the company is wound up` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(3) the member's undertaking covers the winding up` MEANS
    IF `the company is wound up while he is a member`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the date on which he ceases to be a member`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member" (he has not ceased to be a member, and the company is not wound up while he is one)
         WHEN JUST ceased THEN
             IF `the date on which the company is wound up` AT MOST (`add years` ceased 1)
             THEN JUST TRUE -- within one year after he ceases to be a member
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member"

-- src:1342 | (3) The statement of guarantee required to be delivered in the case of a company that is to be limited by guarantee must state that each member undertakes that, if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member, he will contribute to the assets of the company such amount as may be required for—
-- src:1343 | (a) payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member,
-- src:1344 | (b) payment of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up, and
-- src:1345 | (c) adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves,
-- src:1346 | not exceeding a specified amount.
@ref s 106(3) The statement of guarantee: its content (src:1342-1346)
GIVEN `the statement states that each member undertakes that, if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member, he will contribute to the assets of the company such amount as may be required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is for payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is for payment of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is not exceeding a specified amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(3) the statement of guarantee is as required` MEANS
    IF       `the statement states that each member undertakes that, if the company is wound up while he is a member, or within one year after he ceases to be a member, he will contribute to the assets of the company such amount as may be required`
         AND `the amount is for payment of the debts and liabilities of the company contracted before he ceases to be a member`
         AND `the amount is for payment of the costs, charges and expenses of winding up`
         AND `the amount is for adjustment of the rights of the contributories among themselves`
         AND `the amount is not exceeding a specified amount`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of guarantee required to be delivered in the case of a company that is to be limited by guarantee must state that each member undertakes that ..., not exceeding a specified amount."

-- src:1347 | (4) The statement of compliance required to be delivered together with the application is a statement that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a limited company have been complied with.
@ref s 106(4) The statement of compliance (src:1347-1347)
GIVEN `the statement is that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a limited company have been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(4) the statement meets the description of the statement of compliance` MEANS
    IF `the statement is that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a limited company have been complied with`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of compliance ... is a statement that the requirements of this Part as to re-registration as a limited company have been complied with."

-- src:1348 | (5) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a limited company.
@ref s 106(5) The registrar may accept the statement of compliance (src:1348-1348)
GIVEN `a statement of compliance has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 106(5) the registrar may accept the statement of compliance as sufficient evidence that the company is entitled to be re-registered as a limited company` MEANS
    IF `a statement of compliance has been delivered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may accept the statement of compliance"; there is none

-- ---- s 107: issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration -----------------------------------

-- src:1349 | 107 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1350 | (1) If on an application for re-registration of an unlimited company as a limited company the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered, the company shall be re-registered accordingly.
@ref s 107(1) The company shall be re-registered (src:1349-1350)
GIVEN `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(1) the company shall be re-registered as a limited company` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application for re-registration of an unlimited company as a limited company the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered, the company shall be re-registered accordingly."

-- src:1349 | 107 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1351 | (2) The registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 107(2) The registrar must issue a certificate (src:1349-1351)
GIVEN `the company has been re-registered under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(2) the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case` MEANS
    IF `the company has been re-registered under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty follows the re-registration of subsection (1)

-- src:1349 | 107 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1352 | (3) The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is so issued.
@ref s 107(3) What the certificate must state (src:1349-1352)
GIVEN `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states the date on which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(3) the certificate meets the requirement of subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` AND `the certificate states the date on which it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued."

-- src:1349 | 107 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1353 | (4) On the issue of the certificate—
-- src:1354 | (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a limited company, and
@ref s 107(4)(a) The company becomes a limited company on the issue of the certificate (src:1349-1354)
GIVEN `the date on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(4)(a) the company is a limited company on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the certificate is issued`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a limited company" (no certificate has been issued)
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF day AT LEAST issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes a limited company"

-- src:1349 | 107 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1353 | (4) On the issue of the certificate—
-- src:1355 | (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect.
@ref s 107(4)(b) The changes in the company's name and articles take effect (src:1349-1355)
GIVEN `the date on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(4)(b) the changes in the company's name and articles have taken effect on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the certificate is issued`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— ... (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect" (no certificate has been issued)
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF day AT LEAST issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— ... (b) the changes in the company's name and articles take effect"

-- src:1349 | 107 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1356 | (5) The certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Act as to re-registration have been complied with.
@ref s 107(5) The certificate is conclusive evidence (src:1349-1356)
GIVEN `a certificate has been issued on the re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 107(5) the certificate is conclusive evidence that the requirements of this Act as to re-registration have been complied with` MEANS
    IF `a certificate has been issued on the re-registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The certificate is conclusive evidence"; there is no certificate

DECLARE `s 108(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 108(1) deliver a statement of capital to the registrar`

-- src:1357 | 108 Statement of capital required where company already has share capital
-- src:1358 | (1) A company which on re-registration under section 107 already has allotted share capital must within 15 days after the re-registration deliver a statement of capital to the registrar.
-- src:1359 | (2) This does not apply if the information which would be included in the statement has already been sent to the registrar in—
-- src:1360 | (a) a statement of capital and initial shareholdings (see section 10), or
-- src:1361 | (b) (if different) the last statement of capital sent by the company.
@ref s 108(1) A company that already has allotted share capital must deliver a statement of capital within 15 days (and subsection (2)) (src:1357-1361)
GIVEN `the company on re-registration under section 107 already has allotted share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information that would be included in the statement has already been sent to the registrar in a statement of capital and initial shareholdings (see section 10)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information that would be included in the statement has already been sent to the registrar in (if different) the last statement of capital sent by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(1) the company must deliver a statement of capital to the registrar` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the company on re-registration under section 107 already has allotted share capital`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company which on re-registration under section 107 already has allotted share capital"
    ELSE IF       `the information that would be included in the statement has already been sent to the registrar in a statement of capital and initial shareholdings (see section 10)`
              OR  `the information that would be included in the statement has already been sent to the registrar in (if different) the last statement of capital sent by the company`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This does not apply if the information which would be included in the statement has already been sent to the registrar in— (a) ... or (b) ..."
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1357 | 108 Statement of capital required where company already has share capital
-- src:1358 | (1) A company which on re-registration under section 107 already has allotted share capital must within 15 days after the re-registration deliver a statement of capital to the registrar.
@ref s 108(1) The statement of capital is delivered within 15 days after the re-registration (src:1357-1358)
GIVEN `the date of the re-registration` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the statement of capital is delivered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(1) the statement of capital is delivered within 15 days after the re-registration` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the statement of capital is delivered` AT MOST (`the date of the re-registration` PLUS 15)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must within 15 days after the re-registration deliver a statement of capital to the registrar"

-- src:1357 | 108 Statement of capital required where company already has share capital
-- src:1358 | (1) A company which on re-registration under section 107 already has allotted share capital must within 15 days after the re-registration deliver a statement of capital to the registrar.
@ref s 108(1) The duty to deliver a statement of capital within 15 days (src:1357-1358)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 108(1) act`
`s 108(1) the company's duty to deliver a statement of capital` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 108(1) deliver a statement of capital to the registrar`
    WITHIN 15
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company failed to deliver a statement of capital within 15 days after the re-registration: an offence is committed under section 108(4)"

DECLARE `s 108(3) class of shares in the statement` HAS
    `the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares are stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total number of shares of that class is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class is stated` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `s 108(3) statement of capital` HAS
    `the total number of shares of the company is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aggregate nominal value of those shares is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the classes of shares` IS A LIST OF `s 108(3) class of shares in the statement`

-- src:1362 | (3) The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital on re-registration—
-- src:1363 | (a) the total number of shares of the company,
-- src:1364 | (b) the aggregate nominal value of those shares,
-- src:1365 | (ba) the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares (whether on account of their nominal value or by way of premium), and
-- src:1366 | (c) for each class of shares—
-- src:1367 | (i) prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares,
-- src:1368 | (ii) the total number of shares of that class, and
-- src:1369 | (iii) the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class, ...
@ref s 108(3) What the statement of capital must state (src:1362-1369)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 108(3) statement of capital`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(3) the statement of capital states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF       statement's `the total number of shares of the company is stated` -- (a)
         AND statement's `the aggregate nominal value of those shares is stated` -- (b)
         AND statement's `the aggregate amount (if any) unpaid on those shares is stated` -- (ba)
         AND all (GIVEN class YIELD    class's `the prescribed particulars of the rights attached to the shares are stated` -- (c)(i)
                                    AND class's `the total number of shares of that class is stated` -- (c)(ii)
                                    AND class's `the aggregate nominal value of shares of that class is stated`) -- (c)(iii)
                 (statement's `the classes of shares`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The statement of capital must state with respect to the company's share capital on re-registration— (a) ... (b) ... (ba) ... and (c) for each class of shares— (i) ... (ii) ... and (iii) ..."

-- src:1371 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by—
-- src:1372 | (a) the company, and
-- src:1373 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 108(4) Default: who commits the offence (src:1371-1373)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A Party
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108(4) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    IF NOT (`default is made in complying with this section`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN Company THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `Officer in default` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN Director THEN `liability of an officer`
         WHEN `Company secretary` THEN `liability of an officer`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text names the company and every officer in default; it has no sentence treating a shadow director as an officer here
    WHERE
        `liability of an officer` MEANS
            IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

-- src:1374 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 108(5) Offence (penalty) (src:1374-1374)
`s 108(5) the penalty on summary conviction` MEANS
    Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Public company becoming private and unlimited (ss 109-111)
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 109(4) member` HAS
    `the member has assented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a trustee in bankruptcy of the member is entitled to assent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee in bankruptcy has assented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the member is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the personal representative of the deceased member has assented on behalf of the deceased` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1393 | (5) In subsection (4)(a), “a trustee in bankruptcy of a member of the company” includes—
-- src:1394 | (a) a trustee or interim trustee in the sequestration under the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016 of the estate of a member of the company;
-- src:1395 | (b) a trustee under a protected trustee deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016) granted by a member of the company.
@ref s 109(5) "a trustee in bankruptcy of a member" includes (src:1393-1395)
GIVEN `the person is a trustee in bankruptcy of the member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee or interim trustee in the sequestration under the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016 of the estate of a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a trustee under a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016) granted by a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(5) the person is a trustee in bankruptcy of a member of the company` MEANS
    IF       `the person is a trustee in bankruptcy of the member`
         OR  `the person is a trustee or interim trustee in the sequestration under the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016 of the estate of a member of the company`
         OR  `the person is a trustee under a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016) granted by a member of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“a trustee in bankruptcy of a member of the company” includes—"

-- src:1390 | (4) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:1391 | (a) a trustee in bankruptcy of a member of the company is entitled, to the exclusion of the member, to assent to the company's re-registration; and
-- src:1392 | (b) the personal representative of a deceased member of the company may assent on behalf of the deceased.
@ref s 109(4) Who may assent for a member (src:1390-1392)
GIVEN member IS A `s 109(4) member`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(4) the member's assent is given` MEANS
    IF member's `a trustee in bankruptcy of the member is entitled to assent`
    THEN IF member's `the trustee in bankruptcy has assented`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a trustee in bankruptcy of a member of the company is entitled, to the exclusion of the member, to assent to the company's re-registration"
    ELSE IF member's `the member is deceased`
         THEN IF member's `the personal representative of the deceased member has assented on behalf of the deceased`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) all the members of the company have assented to its being so re-registered" (the deceased member's personal representative has not assented on his behalf)
         ELSE IF member's `the member has assented`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) all the members of the company have assented to its being so re-registered"

-- src:1377 | (1) A public company limited by shares may be re-registered as an unlimited private company with a share capital if—
-- src:1378 | (a) all the members of the company have assented to its being so re-registered,
@ref s 109(1)(a) All the members of the company have assented (src:1377-1378)
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `s 109(4) member`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(a) all the members of the company have assented` MEANS
    `s 97(1) all of the answers hold` (map (GIVEN member YIELD `s 109(4) the member's assent is given` member) members)

-- src:1383 | (2) The condition is that the company has not previously been re-registered—
-- src:1384 | (a) as limited, or
-- src:1385 | (b) as unlimited.
@ref s 109(2) The condition (src:1383-1385)
GIVEN `the company has previously been re-registered as limited` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(2) the condition is met` MEANS
    IF `the company has previously been re-registered as limited` OR `the company has previously been re-registered as unlimited`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition is that the company has not previously been re-registered— (a) as limited, or (b) as unlimited."
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:1376 | 109 Re-registration of public company as private and unlimited
-- src:1377 | (1) A public company limited by shares may be re-registered as an unlimited private company with a share capital if—
-- src:1378 | (a) all the members of the company have assented to its being so re-registered,
-- src:1379 | (b) the condition specified below is met, and
-- src:1380 | (c) an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 110, together with—
-- src:1381 | (i) the other documents required by that section, and
-- src:1382 | (ii) a statement of compliance.
@ref s 109(1) Re-registration of public company as private and unlimited (src:1376-1382)
GIVEN `s 4(2) the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 109(1)(a) all the members of the company have assented` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 109(2) the condition is met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 110, together with the other documents required by that section` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of compliance is delivered together with the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1) the public company limited by shares may be re-registered as an unlimited private company with a share capital` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 4(2) the company is a public company` AND `s 3(2) the company is limited by shares`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A public company limited by shares may be re-registered"
    ELSE
        `s 97(1) all of the answers hold`
            (LIST   `s 109(1)(a) all the members of the company have assented`
                  , `s 109(2) the condition is met`
                  , (IF `an application for re-registration is delivered to the registrar in accordance with section 110, together with the other documents required by that section` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE)
                  , (IF `a statement of compliance is delivered together with the application` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE))

