@ref s 111(1) The company shall be re-registered (src:1406-1407)
GIVEN `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(1) the company shall be re-registered as an unlimited private company` MEANS
    IF `the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If on an application for re-registration of a public company as an unlimited private company the registrar is satisfied that the company is entitled to be so re-registered, the company shall be re-registered accordingly."

-- src:1406 | 111 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1408 | (2) The registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case.
