GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(2) the registrar must issue a certificate of incorporation altered to meet the circumstances of the case` MEANS
    IF `the company has been re-registered under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty follows the re-registration of subsection (1)

-- src:1406 | 111 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1409 | (3) The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is so issued.
@ref s 111(3) What the certificate must state (src:1406-1409)
GIVEN `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states the date on which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(3) the certificate meets the requirement of subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF `the certificate states that it is issued on re-registration` AND `the certificate states the date on which it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The certificate must state that it is issued on re-registration and the date on which it is issued."

-- src:1406 | 111 Issue of certificate of incorporation on re-registration
-- src:1410 | (4) On the issue of the certificate—
-- src:1411 | (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes an unlimited private company, and
@ref s 111(4)(a) The company becomes an unlimited private company on the issue of the certificate (src:1406-1411)
GIVEN `the date on which the certificate is issued` IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 111(4)(a) the company is an unlimited private company on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date on which the certificate is issued`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes an unlimited private company" (no certificate has been issued)
    WHEN JUST issued THEN
        IF day AT LEAST issued
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "On the issue of the certificate— (a) the company by virtue of the issue of the certificate becomes an unlimited private company"

